# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("Binding groups and cycles": any line may use any name the block binds, and the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else), Type System ch. 1 and ch. 2: loud gives ((10, !add)), so the label reads "10 10", the button is 1 and the arm's label 2; soft gives 20 and builds nothing in its arm. Never run: prismc refuses the program.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="10 10")
    1: Ui.Button(label="add")
    2: Ui.Label(text="loud")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="20 20")
    1: Ui.Button(label="add")
